{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"Dataset","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int/catalogue/EO:EUM:DAT:MSG:HRSEVIRI-IODC","copyrightHolder":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"copyrightYear":"2017","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"dateCreated":"Sun Jan 01 00:02:00 UTC 2017","dateModified":"Thu Jan 29 00:10:00 UTC 2026","datePublished":"Sun Jan 01 00:02:00 UTC 2017","isAccessibleForFree":"true","keywords":"MSG15,HRSEVIRI-IODC,Weather,Large-scale and synoptic systems,Atmospheric composition,Marine,Mesoscale systems and convective storms,Ocean dynamics,Cloud types","license":"https://www.eumetsat.int/eumetsat-data-licensing","provider":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"schemaVersion":"3.5","spatialCoverage":{"@type":"Place","geo":{"@type":"GeoShape","polygon":"-22  67.5  113  -67.5"}},"temporalCoverage":"Sun Jan 01 00:02:00 UTC 2017 / Thu Jan 29 00:10:00 UTC 2026","thumbnailUrl":"https://user.eumetsat.int/s3/eup-strapi-media/L1_5_channel_7_8a6f66a75f.png","encodingFormat":"HRIT","description":"Rectified (level 1.5) Meteosat SEVIRI image data. The data is transmitted as High Rate transmissions in 12 spectral channels. L1.5 image data corresponds to the geolocated and radiometrically pre-processed image data, ready for further processing, eg, the extraction of meteorological products. Any spacecraft specific effects have been removed, and in particular, linearisation and equalisation of the image radiometry has been performed for all SEVIRI channels. The on-board blackbody data has been processed. Both radiometric and geometric quality control information is included.

Images are made available with different timeliness according to their latency: quarter-hourly images if latency is more than 3 hours and hourly images if latency is less than 3 hours (for a total of 87 images per day). To enhance the perception for areas which are on the night side of the Earth a different mapping with increased contrast is applied for IR3.9 product. The greyscale mapping is based on the EBBT which allows to map the ranges 200 K to 300 K for the night and 250 K to 330 K for the day. A selection of single channel data are visualised in our EUMETView service.

From 1 June 2022, Meteosat-9 at 45.5° E is the prime satellite for the IODC service, replacing Meteosat-8 (located at 41.5° E while in operation).","identifier":"EO:EUM:DAT:MSG:HRSEVIRI-IODC","name":"High Rate SEVIRI Level 1.5 Image Data - MSG - Indian Ocean"}

{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"Dataset","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int/catalogue/EO:EUM:DAT:0862","copyrightHolder":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"copyrightYear":"2023","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"dateCreated":"Wed Jan 04 00:05:00 UTC 2023","dateModified":"Thu Jan 29 00:10:00 UTC 2026","datePublished":"Wed Jan 04 00:05:00 UTC 2023","isAccessibleForFree":"true","keywords":"AVHGAC1C0100,Climate,Climate system monitoring - Atmosphere,NWP-based reanalysis","license":"https://www.eumetsat.int/eumetsat-data-licensing","provider":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"schemaVersion":"3.5","spatialCoverage":{"@type":"Place","geo":{"@type":"GeoShape","polygon":"-180  90  180  -90"}},"temporalCoverage":"Wed Jan 04 00:05:00 UTC 2023 / Thu Jan 29 00:10:00 UTC 2026","thumbnailUrl":"https://user.eumetsat.int/s3/eup-strapi-media/pygac_fdr_r1_2_a2d95338d0.png","encodingFormat":"netCDF4","description":"This AVHRR Fundamental Data Record (FDR) consists of reflectance and brightness temperatures. The FDR was homogeneously produced for a period ranging from 1978 – 2021 using PyGAC (a Python software package to read, calibrate and navigate AVHRR data in GAC format). It is based on observations from 17 AVHRR instruments on board NOAA satellites TIROS-N to NOAA-19, as well as EUMETSAT satellites Metop-A, -B, and -C. For calibration the PATMOS-X calibration coefficients have been applied to visible channels and the nominal operational calibration has been used for the infrared channels.

The polygons, required for the data tailoring (area of interest selection), show problems with non-continues data. Some polygons of the data record are found to be incorrect. This only affects the geographical area selection, but does not affect the correctness of the data itself.

On the 28 October 2024, the dataset was extended to cover the period of 2022 until June 2024 (satellites Metop-B, Metop-C, NOAA-15, NOAA-18, NOAA-19). Note that as part of this extension, the entire Metop-C record was reprocessed with improved calibration coefficients from PATMOS-X.","identifier":"EO:EUM:DAT:0862","name":"AVHRR Fundamental Data Record - Release 1 - Multimission"}

